---
layout: base.njk
title: null
description: "A personal journal of articles, statistical analyses, and projects — starting with a rating system for college football players."
---
{% from "article-card.njk" import card %}
<section class="wrap hero">
  <h1 class="hero__title">Writing, statistics, and projects — worked on in the open.</h1>
  <p class="hero__lede">
    Carney Journal is a personal publication where I post original articles, statistical
    analyses, and side projects as I work on them. Most pieces start as rough working
    papers and get revised over time. Sports analytics is the current focus, but the
    scope will widen as new interests show up.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="wrap section">
  <div class="section__head">
    <h2>Latest</h2>
    <a href="/articles/">All articles &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid">
    {% for article in collections.articles | limit(6) %}
      {{ card(article) }}
    {% else %}
      <p class="empty">No articles published yet — the first one is on its way.</p>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap section section--about">
  <h2>About this journal</h2>
  <p>
    I'm a first-year college student, and this site is where I publish work as I make it —
    including the early, unpolished stuff. Pieces are labeled as <strong>working papers</strong>,
    <strong>drafts</strong>, or <strong>finished</strong> so it's clear how far along something is.
    Read more on the <a href="/about/">About page</a>.
  </p>
</section>
